, J. L. (2021). Behavioral and psychological treatments for chronic insomnia disorder in adults: An American Academy of Sleep Medicine clinical practice guideline. Journal of Clinical Sleep Medicine, 17(2), 255–262. https://doi.org/10.5664/jcsm.8986","Kuula, L., Halonen, R., Kajanto, K., Lipsanen, J., Makkonen, T., Peltonen, M., & Pesonen, A.-K. (2020). The effects of presleep slow breathing and music listening on polysomnographic sleep measures — a pilot trial. Scientific Reports, 10(1), 7427. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-64218-7","Balban, M. Y., Neri, E., Kogon, M. M., Weed, L., Nouriani, B., Jo, B., Holl, G., Zeitzer, J. M., Spiegel, D., & Huberman, A. D. (2023). Brief structured respiration practices enhance mood and reduce physiological arousal. Cell Reports Medicine, 4(1), 100895. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xcrm.2022.100895"],"min":25,"over":false},{"rec":false,"area":"Sleep","fam":"Bedtime to-do list","action":"Write a to-do list for the next few days before bed","freq":"for 5 minutes every night","start":"Write down the tasks you need to remember, and make each item as specific as you can.","why":"A quick to-do list clears your mind so you can drift off more easily.","refs":["Scullin, M. K., Krueger, M. L., Ballard, H. K., Pruett, N., & Bliwise, D. L. (2018). The effects of bedtime writing on difficulty falling asleep: A polysomnographic study comparing to-do lists and completed activity lists. Journal of Experimental Psychology: General, 147(1), 139–146. https://doi.org/10.1037/xge0000374"],"min":35,"over":false}],"mins":0,"lower":60,"timeTxt":"1–2 hours","pace":"A bigger challenge","optout":[],"planned":true,"steps":{"m2":[{"area":"Sleep","fam":"Bedtime music","action":"Listen to calm music at bedtime to help you wind down","freq":"for 25–45 minutes, 5 nights a week","start":"Set a sleep timer so the music switches off on its own.","min":0,"refs":["Jespersen, K. V., Pando-Naude, V., Koenig, J., Jennum, P., & Vuust, P. (2022). Listening to music for in